[{:db/id "q-49221/selection/6597015b60bd18b5b5b58ac7a65569c48c6aa4cd468847566bb695a6890ad949" :answer/id #uuid "b5542d14-dcdf-564d-897b-10378ad37a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49221/selection/776cfe34741a7794d0066f9f9c54a5e877c407ff565956b7644804cfa99b9ccc" :answer/id #uuid "9dbc1e75-7e1e-5bda-94ac-210323be8178" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49221/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "8b229a58-2050-51cc-bf07-afba7ceef4d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49221/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "220df84e-67c2-58aa-b797-090807b18afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49221/selection/b4b6873f65ca812307b6fac9df14533b775f5e800dbac0876854af425fe29ad3" :answer/id #uuid "6d66c22e-26c8-556e-9aaa-2f626618e473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49221/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b772302-6f9f-5cb9-b920-a2693f43f64f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49221/selection/6597015b60bd18b5b5b58ac7a65569c48c6aa4cd468847566bb695a6890ad949" :answer-field/choices ["q-49221/selection/6597015b60bd18b5b5b58ac7a65569c48c6aa4cd468847566bb695a6890ad949" "q-49221/selection/776cfe34741a7794d0066f9f9c54a5e877c407ff565956b7644804cfa99b9ccc" "q-49221/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-49221/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-49221/selection/b4b6873f65ca812307b6fac9df14533b775f5e800dbac0876854af425fe29ad3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49221" :question/id #uuid "49bb0d44-38eb-57b0-b09a-35f77b00b9ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-49221" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{(-2)}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{(-1)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(-4)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15bd1f67-6361-55f7-ba25-07e54aad8f66"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342591/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "08d80e3c-2f4b-54fa-bc59-8271c54ea8b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342591/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b80233ac-f41c-57d6-b390-29647f4da7e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342591/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-342591/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342591" :question/id #uuid "97e97885-5364-548d-a866-b48f29ce6c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-342591" :question/problem "Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(-2)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $-2$ | $-3$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $7$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(-2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(-2)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-2))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(-2)=5$ and ${f}^{′}(5)=-3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(-2) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342591/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911/selection/23df3cc8fd5bde0e386e55c7795c32c23c3fa77f1d5949a3eb5b26ccfe49a47a" :answer/id #uuid "0033bc47-e537-5394-8f40-841d466de5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911/selection/7a6d1d176b8642a56f2603d0a83dd054a16eb31e70d87fe78ade2a39774ad414" :answer/id #uuid "2ecbea32-ea9d-5a56-b13f-bde8e585ba41" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911/selection/f731efd3c86e79bd1ec82599defe86bf97299cbd1a69ebcdb5508161f7a441f2" :answer/id #uuid "71fcf031-cf94-59f8-874a-5a745b2953aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911/selection/96ab28642cc20567e68c5b109ee2709ff210e70a66df114355b78b2b8f331677" :answer/id #uuid "1e18b132-a788-5718-a65a-02fd187ee966" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911/selection/c00b423d38fc022695304b5623f8f16d80f952174b860c25dbbf7c6f3e0429ea" :answer/id #uuid "84767ecd-933a-5540-b2f5-a5e0d11c176f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "594f89de-b0ea-5b81-84f5-a93099ab18f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47911/selection/f731efd3c86e79bd1ec82599defe86bf97299cbd1a69ebcdb5508161f7a441f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-47911/selection/23df3cc8fd5bde0e386e55c7795c32c23c3fa77f1d5949a3eb5b26ccfe49a47a" "q-47911/selection/7a6d1d176b8642a56f2603d0a83dd054a16eb31e70d87fe78ade2a39774ad414" "q-47911/selection/f731efd3c86e79bd1ec82599defe86bf97299cbd1a69ebcdb5508161f7a441f2" "q-47911/selection/96ab28642cc20567e68c5b109ee2709ff210e70a66df114355b78b2b8f331677" "q-47911/selection/c00b423d38fc022695304b5623f8f16d80f952174b860c25dbbf7c6f3e0429ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47911" :question/id #uuid "cfc1f38a-b4e3-5848-bc27-d254a3cdbd67" :question/math-academy-id "q-47911" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/bb8959927fc561f9fc6e021b690c43f4ab57b169aa1526390e02c8d48386bfe3.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?" :question/worked-solution "The critical points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist. Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal or where the tangent does not exist, respectively. \n\nIn the given graph, we can see that \n\n- at $x=2$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(0)=0,$ while\n\n- at $x=4$ there is a sharp corner, so ${f}^{′}(4)$ doesn't exist\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/60f26a8aa758ae20b2b56325d822379d407276ffd6987f56a1e7934a6406c4d2.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there are two critical points, and their $x$-coordinates are $x=2$ and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47911/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47911"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274/selection/7de92e9b64a1a978d42c5865b938cead1f2ec4d1f4df5332e44b3c958139a5d7" :answer/id #uuid "e1f7479f-7f79-5184-bc71-130f64f3e07b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1<x<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274/selection/90e25cb50458be1836937a7c3656bf5c74eb916db22c58527a637a0761b26868" :answer/id #uuid "45e14bd3-d5b4-5f08-87a1-f70494cd1f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-4$ or $x>1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274/selection/6686dfb73c90dde3ddf2bc8c9eb7c43a7ef84f0f62e6436768ae86871fdd1c2b" :answer/id #uuid "e7c390cf-4cd1-50f5-800b-879fea95f549" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-1$ or $x>4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" :answer/id #uuid "d7374576-071a-5fa1-8521-87a67d55ea2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274/selection/79a9cadc6f3dcfc8b339ae85edf4ff4828e22819c5e099dbf1876fb476e8f1d1" :answer/id #uuid "8c61ba4a-50b5-5548-a6bb-235cc6daf555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4<x<-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8ff6265-a9a6-5700-a27d-6a1a7e781291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115274/selection/6686dfb73c90dde3ddf2bc8c9eb7c43a7ef84f0f62e6436768ae86871fdd1c2b" :answer-field/choices ["q-115274/selection/7de92e9b64a1a978d42c5865b938cead1f2ec4d1f4df5332e44b3c958139a5d7" "q-115274/selection/90e25cb50458be1836937a7c3656bf5c74eb916db22c58527a637a0761b26868" "q-115274/selection/6686dfb73c90dde3ddf2bc8c9eb7c43a7ef84f0f62e6436768ae86871fdd1c2b" "q-115274/selection/c4d8fcc3d0001d305927fbe8d5a0bcc565b987d26bf192f936c7579b4dde886a" "q-115274/selection/79a9cadc6f3dcfc8b339ae85edf4ff4828e22819c5e099dbf1876fb476e8f1d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115274" :question/id #uuid "73608df6-a2a9-5efe-b3f4-d968a8f235fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-115274" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/402ae2f9f3d1e0ce970a18b68332400d261962e40ebde9acdc179727e94f32ac.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality  $(x+1)(x-4)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+1)(x-4)>0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=(x+1)(x-4)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/98537a1ab5afd590c47a2605d6d0bc8858f51e838033cc61a38845b3e8c87a53.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-1$ or $x>4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115274/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eec195c-6549-5de2-b3f0-0417e5f518e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115274"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-302331/field-1/0d493251931cc605e892db74e058983a8bd88db494d0e39af4dca97c0964b1b2" :answer/id #uuid "41956e2e-8d3a-56ed-b519-8d3967b79417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302331/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfe93357-b04f-50e0-bc40-5cc2c2c4bcb4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302331/field-1/0d493251931cc605e892db74e058983a8bd88db494d0e39af4dca97c0964b1b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-302331/field-1/0d493251931cc605e892db74e058983a8bd88db494d0e39af4dca97c0964b1b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302331" :question/id #uuid "56ee2d50-7525-539b-8670-a399c4adf79c" :question/math-academy-id "q-302331" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=3$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{3}} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{3}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-9)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{3})}{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{3})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{3})}{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{3})}{x-3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-3)}(x+3)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{3})}{\\cancel{x-3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}(x+3)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =(3+3)(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =6(2\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-302331/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302331"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321410/field-1/9333865b78cc000fbd6d505ffc59276d3fea3a9430dfd87d42ff49f92c856d89" :answer/id #uuid "c8840ae0-7cbf-521d-b355-e1b29f10030a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321410/field-1/fdd3dcc9586e80436a653292c8c3c365a633b1c3e157585e2b0e371a2cefaafe" :answer/id #uuid "03109a29-2a80-586b-b64f-c5695518e8a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321410/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "745fea25-6d62-5921-9c24-a67f3114aeab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321410/field-1/9333865b78cc000fbd6d505ffc59276d3fea3a9430dfd87d42ff49f92c856d89" :answer-field/choices ["q-321410/field-1/9333865b78cc000fbd6d505ffc59276d3fea3a9430dfd87d42ff49f92c856d89" "q-321410/field-1/fdd3dcc9586e80436a653292c8c3c365a633b1c3e157585e2b0e371a2cefaafe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321410/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "25a7fd8d-e163-50ff-851f-0ac51b5dbaee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321410/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c98a97b5-6183-5310-9855-2bb3c4c205aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321410/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-321410/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321410" :question/id #uuid "032b7386-bebf-584d-aa51-c55bac49aec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-321410" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-3t+2,\\,\\,\\,y=-\\frac{1}{t},\\,t\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ne $\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3t+2\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{2-x}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{2-x}{3}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{2-x}{3})} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{3}{x-2}.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ne 0$ and $x=-3t+2$ , we must have $x\\ne 2.$ \n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{x-2},\\,x\\ne 2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321410/field-1" "q-321410/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79107609-77e6-55e9-970d-da63c39daf0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321410"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-147603"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/0cec723bf4e6886ca0715e9e02c658a7ee0e1f24555ea3946f95aa2b12b863be.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,2)$, $(-2,2),$ $(2,-2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/c688b1ee540e732329e597fb97a0595f619dbc4ff0aad86b6a01f1bdb51ae66b.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-87125"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059760/assets/c010f583fc33ee3c5335c16c0aaf1c20c2e5cf82d49fe7cf14e8e5661bf202fc.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the ray shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607/selection/c734e3315c3c2867d6eaaf80433d198ffd3df008a4bc1c57364b5b4162651a70" :answer/id #uuid "e89eeffb-1442-5ad9-8c7e-466d35845290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607/selection/ca7856e0dfa6df97b10305d6bfc00095dfda382575d9e7c7025fcbaaa67fb80d" :answer/id #uuid "131f526d-0f02-57ba-9efd-0f15ea3a3905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607/selection/f2ce4ea96f3c950e5c989127a64aa12f52cbc84cfdc7f11767a7027773d879c4" :answer/id #uuid "d94e3891-28c7-5c24-b058-d0e91d5957a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607/selection/61255f70350d048dbf32d24549be7bb64b9ec159c8218658dc0fbd33fff2f183" :answer/id #uuid "74876d33-40ef-5630-9a88-6a3381c99893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607/selection/214d4d635869b412d3cfc0b3de6498f92000540547fc7a46da8eaa44bbcb7254" :answer/id #uuid "c9627a6e-c790-5025-b101-12ea1591e8fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a65eb51-3516-5f48-b5a6-84c50f962faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113607/selection/f2ce4ea96f3c950e5c989127a64aa12f52cbc84cfdc7f11767a7027773d879c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-113607/selection/c734e3315c3c2867d6eaaf80433d198ffd3df008a4bc1c57364b5b4162651a70" "q-113607/selection/ca7856e0dfa6df97b10305d6bfc00095dfda382575d9e7c7025fcbaaa67fb80d" "q-113607/selection/f2ce4ea96f3c950e5c989127a64aa12f52cbc84cfdc7f11767a7027773d879c4" "q-113607/selection/61255f70350d048dbf32d24549be7bb64b9ec159c8218658dc0fbd33fff2f183" "q-113607/selection/214d4d635869b412d3cfc0b3de6498f92000540547fc7a46da8eaa44bbcb7254"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113607" :question/id #uuid "31c261c0-c13d-56df-97d3-69bf96671591" :question/math-academy-id "q-113607" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2})+[]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{6}) \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
